# proto-file: intrinsic/world/public/proto/object_world_updates.proto
# proto-message: intrinsic_proto.world.ObjectWorldUpdates

# Application (software) joint position limits for the UR5e of the OMTS cell.
#
# wrist_3_joint (joint 6) carries the gripper and camera cabling, so its
# rotation is restricted to [-210 deg, +220 deg] instead of the UR5e default of
# +/- 356.4 deg.
#
# intrinsic_proto.JointLimitsUpdate replaces a limit field as a whole, so all
# six joints have to be listed in kinematic order even though only
# wrist_3_joint deviates from the UR5e defaults in
# @intrinsic-core//intrinsic_control/intrinsic/models/robot_definitions/ur:
# ur5e/ur5e_limits.updates.pbtxt (95% of the system limits). Velocity,
# acceleration, jerk, and effort limits are left unset and therefore keep
# those defaults.
updates {
  update_object_joints {
    object {
      by_name {
        object_name: "ur_module"
      }
    }
    joint_application_limits {
      min_position {
        values: -6.2203534  # shoulder_pan_joint
        values: -4.059      # shoulder_lift_joint
        values: -2.772      # elbow_joint
        values: -6.2203534  # wrist_1_joint
        values: -6.2203534  # wrist_2_joint
        values: -3.6651914  # wrist_3_joint (-210 deg)
      }
      max_position {
        values: 6.2203534  # shoulder_pan_joint
        values: 0.9504     # shoulder_lift_joint
        values: 2.772      # elbow_joint
        values: 6.2203534  # wrist_1_joint
        values: 6.2203534  # wrist_2_joint
        values: 3.8397244  # wrist_3_joint (+220 deg)
      }
    }
  }
}
